rota lap 4333, row 3 -- Water, the row that tastes; its cardinal seat (what-brix-infuse-is) instructs a lap to RUN tools/c/convergence_census.sh rather than quote the sentence about it, and running it is what found the fault in the reading
think At the open the runner refused: an orphaned --hot pass held construction/standing-equipment-run.lock.d, pid 277235, parent exited, output reaching nobody. /proc/277235/cwd resolved to this tree, so kill -TERM ran the runner's own EXIT trap and released the lock, exactly as its refusal message instructs. Thirty seconds.
think The water seat asks what a round changed and whether running it again would change more. Its instrument is tools/c/convergence_census.sh; it answered candidates=7 over tools_read=3244.
think Reading the seven found the fault in the reading itself. The census's writer predicate greps a write, then applies a pen-name exclusion and a tree-path inclusion to the WHOLE matched span. A write has a source and a target, and testing the span lets either answer for both.
think Proven on metal: printf 'cat "$tmp" > "$LEDGER"' matches the write pattern, then falls to grep -vE on the $tmp sitting to the LEFT of the arrow. That shape is what .claude/rules/exec-bit.md prescribes, since writing through the original inode preserves the mode the repository tracks -- so the census was blind to exactly the writes this tree's own law requires.
think Four writers were dropped that way, and two of them are tools/fixtures/r/readme_metrics_splice.sh and tools/fixtures/r/reds_ledger_headline_write.sh, which tools/hooks/pre-commit runs on every commit and every amend. The busiest writing this tree does stood outside the census that measures whether writing converges.
think The same span reading ran the other way: tools/fixtures/d/dated_classify_seam.sh was ADMITTED on a "$f" that was a printf's SOURCE while its target was the scratch $resc. One fault, two directions, and the fifth wrong denominator after 392, 1200, 30 and 7.
think The repair extracts each match's target -- the last quoted run, which serves both the redirect shape and the sed in-place shape -- and applies both tests to the target alone. 7 -> 10 candidates, 3 -> 5 proven, one false positive out and four false negatives in.
think reds_ledger_headline_write.sh does converge in fact: it returns changed=no before reaching its stamp rewrite when the three headline numbers already agree. The property holds and nothing asserts it, which is the census's own sentence -- the promise is kept where a hand happened to remember.
obs Against myself, first: my repair's own header prose spelled ca[t] "$tmp" > "$f" whole, so the census counted ITSELF and its witness -- 10 candidates reading 12, a scan counting a mention as a use, inside the paragraph that warns about it. Caught by running the census after editing rather than by rereading the edit. Cured with the dodge the file already used for sed -[i], and the reason written down beside it.
obs Against myself, second: I edited a tracked file while the cold roster pass was running, against the card's own hold-still directive, so that pass closes tree_moved. The hot pass over the staged set is the receipt this commit ships.
obs The control is the half that matters. Four of the five wrong denominators shipped with no control at all; tools/fixtures/c/convergence_census_control.sh plants each shape in real git repositories and runs the ELDER predicate over the same plants, asserting it disagrees on exactly the two legs the repair moves -- because a repair shown only in the passing direction reads the same as a coincidence.
obs Claimed across lanes: tools/c/ is not amphora or bron-resins. My lane's agent-doable queue held gates only -- the pin, and a question for Keaton about the doorway family's rooms.
obs Against myself, third and fourth, and the hot pass is what caught them. My new account shelf carried the two links its elder block wrote relative to construction/, so inside construction/archive/ they resolved to archive/archive/ and reddened fold_shelf_link and fold_shelf_link_repoint -- the exact trap BAKERY described on this card, which I read at the open. And my control planted the literal GNU in-place flag, which shell_dialect walls at zero across tracked sources since BSD sed needs an argument after it; a file planting one reads as a file using one. Both repaired: the shelf links dropped their archive/ prefix, and the flag is composed at runtime with a comment saying why. All four witnesses re-run GREEN.
obs Hot pass: guards_run=197, guards_seconds=1762, guards_green=187, guards_red=7, guards_gated=3, tree_moved=no. Four of the seven reds were mine and all four are closed; the remaining three are seed_link (a peer's README link to context/BHAKTA_STYLE.md, a room the seed manifest does not carry, landed at 2587f79f1), stash_record (%636), and standing_equipment's pen leg (%549).
obs Cold pass: guards_run=197, guards_seconds=1832, guards_green=191, guards_red=3, tree_moved=yes -- the tree_moved is mine, from editing tools/c/convergence_census.sh while it ran.
obs The pin refused this red: pin_headroom=24, pin_open_rows=13, rows_that_fit=0, pin_deadlocked=1. A fourth ship in one day. The row is named by stamp on the card instead.
